    "https://www.urmedicine.org/locations/highlands-at-brighton/jobs.cfm": {
      "title": "Better health, driven by discovery",
      "description": "University of Rochester Medicine | URochester Medicine Skip\r\n    to content Common Searches MyChart Login On-Demand Video Visits Remote Access Jobs Quick Links Find\r\n                                                a Provider Cost\r\n                                                    Estimator Clinical\r\n                                                        Trials Refer a Patient MyChart Pay a Bill Cost Estimates & Pricing Careers Giving Research Education Community Health Find a Provider Locations Conditions & Treatments Get Care Now Search MyChart Pay a Bill Cost Estimates & Pricing Careers Giving Research Education Community Health Better health, driven by discovery We're the leading academic health system in Upstate New York, connecting patient care with innovation and education to advance health every day, in every way. Get Care ﻿ Advancing Health. Enriching Lives. University of Rochester Medicine unites our entire health system—hospitals, providers, research, and education—under a single, trusted name. It’s a clearer, more connected experience designed to make your care easier at every step. Explore Our Brand ﻿ Get & Manage Care Get Care Now Whenever and wherever you need care, we’re there for you. Find emergency, urgent, and virtual care options. View Care Options ﻿ MyChart Your online portal to make appointments, view test results, eCheck-in, read notes from your provider, and more. Log in to MyChart ﻿ Pay Bills Online View your bill and pay it, pay by phone, or set up recurring payments so no bill is left unpaid. Pay a Bill ﻿ World-Class Cancer Care Clinical Trials - Searching for Cures Faced with an extremely rare diagnosis, Meghan placed her trust with the experts at Wilmot Cancer Institute. Her journey illustrates her resilience and how being treated at an NCI-designated cancer center can make all the difference. Find a Clinical Trial ﻿ Backed by Research Our 3,000+ researchers turn breakthroughs into care that improves lives every day. See how discovery becomes real here. Research Programs Steve Dewhurst, Vice President for Research \"Our research impacts patient care on a daily basis, and that's because our clinicians are deeply involved in our research effort and vice versa. It's that synergy that lies at the heart of this academic medical center, and it's what sets us apart.\" A New Kind of Education Our School of Medicine & Dentistry weaves classroom and clinical learning through all four years of learning. Graduate Medical Education offers more than 90 programs across numerous disciplines. Our School of Nursing offers options for all types of students, including career changers. The Eastman Institute of Oral Health attracts postdoc dental students and residents from around the world. Education Programs Cassandra Houser ('22) | Microbiology & Immunology \"What caught me and caught my attention about Rochester was the people. When I interviewed I had very positive interactions with not only the faculty, but the students. Of course, the research was cutting edge, but definitely the people is what brought me to Rochester.\" Health Equity and Community Health Our goal is equal life expectancy for all in our community. See how partnerships, new initiatives, and training of clinicians and scientists are transforming how we operate and deliver care. Health Equity in Action Latest Stories & News Aug. 31, 2026 Hidden Immune Cells in the Lung Could Lead to Better Flu Vaccines Aug. 27, 2026 Heart Palpitations: When They're Normal—and When to See a Doctor Aug. 24, 2026 School Year Stress: Acing the Back-to-School Season Sign up for our newsletter for weekly updates! Sign Up About URochester Medicine Newsroom Contact Us Notice of Privacy Practices Patient & Visitor Resources Clinical Trials Closings & Cancellations Events Health Encyclopedia Medical Records Price Transparency For Medical Professionals For Employees Notice of Non-Discrimination Policy Policies Follow Us: ©2026  University of Rochester Medical Center"
    },
    "https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/home-care/careers.aspx": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers - UR Medicine Home Care - URochester Medicine Skip to main content Home Healthcare menu About Us Health Home Nurse-Family Partnership Patient Feedback Services & Specialty Programs Home Care Services Pediatric and Perinatal Services Specialty Programs Hospice Care Meals On Wheels More information on Services & Specialty Programs News & Events For Physicians Home Care Referral Form Hospice Referral Form Physician Newsletter More information for Physicians Contact Us Giving About Us How to Give How We Use Your Gift Ways to Help Donating FAQs More information on Giving Careers A Great Place to Work We Are Hiring! View All Current Job Openings Home Care / Careers Careers Find your way home—to an agency that cares like family At University of Rochester Medicine Home Healthcare, home isn’t just where we provide care—it’s how we make people feel. That includes our patients, their families, and our team members. We invite you to Find Your Way Home to a team that supports your growth, values your contributions, and empowers you to make a meaningful impact every day. Why Work With Us? Feel supported by leaders who know you and have your back. Feel balanced with flexible schedules and time to breathe. Feel appreciated with generous PTO and great pay & benefits. Feel proud knowing your work makes a difference. Feel confident with opportunities to grow, learn, and reach your potential—your way. Ready to join our team? Explore our current openings and discover how you and your career can thrive at Home Healthcare. View All Current Job Openings Most In-Demand Roles Registered Nurse - Home Care Hospice Registered Nurse Physical Therapist Registered Nurse - Weekend Physical Therapist - Finger Lakes Comprehensive Benefit Offering: Medical Benefits 5 medical plans to choose from, co-pay and hybrid plans and 3 high-deductible health plans Company pays from 65-92% of premiums, depending on plan and tier Significant company contribution to Health Saving Accounts (HSA) - from 50-100% of each plan’s deductible contributed to employees HSAs Dental plan through MetLife.  Company contributes to the premiums Vision –2 options offered; Davis and VSP, for you to be able to select the plan that best meets your needs Flexible Spending Accounts Medical Dependent Care Limited Purpose (dental & vision) Financial Benefits 401k (Pre-tax and Roth) with company contribution Tuition Assistance Program ICARE funding for training and staff development PTO Benefits Generous Paid Time Off – up to 43 days total in a year! Vacation up to 22 days Personal Time up to 4 days 7 Sick Days 9 Holidays, plus Veterans Day if you are a Veteran *Days are defined as 8 hours Up to 5 days Bereavement Time Paid Family Leave and Paid Sick/Safe Leave Additional Benefits Company paid Life Insurance Voluntary Life Insurance (in addition to company paid life insurance) Voluntary Short-Term Disability (in addition to NYS Disability) Long Term Disability – company contributes 20% towards premium Accident Insurance – company contributes 20% towards premium Critical Illness Insurance Hospital Indemnity Insurance Mileage reimbursement at IRS recommended rate Employee Referral Program Employee Assistance Program Home and Auto Insurance exclusive savings Pet Insurance Employer Assisted Housing Program Roadside Assistance Program For visiting, patient facing staff Reasonable productivity expectations Mileage counts toward productivity Meetings count toward productivity Flexibility in patient scheduling Home Healthcare Patient Rights Privacy Policies Contact Us Toll Free: 1-800-253-4439 Local: (585) 787-2233 Webster 2180 Empire Boulevard Webster, NY 14580 ©2026 University of Rochester Medical Center Rochester, NY Intranet Email myURHR Remote Access (VPN) Privacy Topics Viewing: UrmcWebTest"
    },
    "http://www.thompsonhealth.com/CareerbrOpportunities/CareerOpportunities.aspx": {
      "title": "Our Benefits",
      "description": "Thompson Health Careers MyChart Pay a Bill Donate News Physician Opportunities Nursing Opportunities Cost Estimator Search Toggle Search Search Providers, locations, conditions, etc. Common Searches MyChart Login On-Demand Video Visits Remote Access Jobs Quick Links Find a Provider Cost Estimator Clinical Trials Refer a Patient Menu Health Services Back to Health Services Birthing Center Back to Birthing Center Birthing Center Classes Breastfeeding Support Videos for New Parents Cardio and Pulmonary Service Back to Cardio and Pulmonary Service Cardiac Rehabilitation Diagnostic Imaging Back to Diagnostic Imaging Computed Tomography (CT) Interventional Radiology Mammography Nuclear Medicine X-ray Ultrasound MRI Breast MRI Diagnostic Imaging Forms Bone Density Breast Imaging Center Dialysis / Nephrology Services Emergency Medicine Back to Emergency Medicine Urgent Care Urgent, ED or Primary Care? Where to Go Gastroenterology Intensive Care Laboratory Medicine Medical Nutrition Therapy Back to Medical Nutrition Therapy Bariatric Surgery Program Dietitian Nutrition Corner Observation Unit Obstetrics and Gynecology Back to Obstetrics and Gynecology OB-GYN Ultrasound Cancer Genetic Testing Gynecologic Surgery What is a Certified Nurse Midwife? Occupational Medicine | HealthWorks Back to Occupational Medicine | HealthWorks HealthWorks Forms Industrial Rehab Services Occupational Health Services Workplace Safety Orthopaedic Surgery Pain Management Pediatrics Pharmacy Primary Care Back to Primary Care Be Proactive Primary Care Practices FAQ Billing & Insurance Info Patient-Centered Medical Homes Canandaigua Family Practice Canandaigua Medical Group Internal Medicine Farmington Medical Group Family Medicine Finger Lakes Family Care Honeoye Family Practice Lima Family Practice Macedon Family Practice The Mary Clark Thompson Family Practice Midlakes Family Practice Pediatrics Shortsville Family Practice Victor Family Practice Primary Care New Patient Pulmonary Services Back to Pulmonary Services Pulmonary Clinic Pulmonary Rehabilitation Rehabilitation Services Back to Rehabilitation Services Farmington Rehabilitation Victor Rehabilitation Physical Therapy Occupational Therapy Aquatic Therapy Athletic Training Hand Therapy Lymphedema Therapy Pelvic-Women's Health Therapy Speech Therapy TMD Rehabilitation Vertigo Treatment Rehab Staff Sands Cancer Center Sleep Disorders Stroke Center at F.F. Thompson Hospital Back to Stroke Center at F.F. Thompson Hospital Learn About Stroke Stroke Support Group Surgical Services Back to Surgical Services General Surgery Breast Cancer Surgery Corneal Transplants Hernia Surgery Vascular Surgery For Patients Urgent Care Patients & Visitors Back to Patients & Visitors Patient Guide Back to Patient Guide Coming to the Hospital While You're Here Going Home LGBTQ Patients Patient Rights Your Bill National Healthcare Decisions Day Visitors Advance Directives Visitor Information Caring Bridge Comfort & Convenience Billing & Insurance Back to Billing & Insurance Cost Estimates & Pricing Financial Aid Your Insurance & NY State Out of Network Law General Info Gift Shop & Flowers Medical Records Back to Medical Records FAQs Parking Smoke Free Social Work Spiritual Care Support Groups Star Catcher Discharge with Dignity Visitation Policy Education Back to Education Calendar of Events & Classes Athletic Training Corner Birthing Classes Ovarian Cancer Donate Life Partners In Health and Wellness Thompson On-Air Podcast Quit Smoking Support Groups Stroke Wellness Briefs Senior Living Back to Senior Living M.M. Ewing Continuing Care Center Back to M.M. Ewing Continuing Care Center Post Hospital Services Dementia Care Long Term Services M.M. Ewing Admissions CCC - About Us Ferris Hills at West Lake Clark Meadows Back to Clark Meadows Short Stay Resources Map & Directions Foundation Back to Foundation Board of Directors Donating Honor Your Doctor Mary Clark Thompson Grants Back to Mary Clark Thompson Grants MCT Grant Recipients Publications Planning a Fundraiser Planned Giving Special Events Back to Special Events Thompson Health Golf Classic Thompson Health Gala Thompson Guild Back to Thompson Guild Tree of Lights Guild Gallery Gift Shops Guild History Join the Guild Guild's Scholarship Guild Fashion Show Volunteering Opt-out Event Photo Gallery Careers Back to Careers Careers Nursing Back to Nursing Daisy Bee Award Nursing at Thompson Health CNA Apprentice Program CNA Job Openings Physician Back to Physician OB/GYN Physician Opportunities Family Medicine Physician Opportunity Benefits Back to Benefits Badge Replacement Student Back to Student Career Exploration Day 2026 Volunteer Back to Volunteer Volunteer Application Locations Associate Referral Our Stories About Us Back to About Us Message from the CEO Awards and Recognitions Board of Directors History Mission, Vision & Values News Room Back to News Room Press Releases Publications Events Calendar Smoke Free Our Community Map & Directions Contact Us Privacy Legal and Regulatory Affairs Department Back to Legal and Regulatory Affairs Department Integrity Helpline Vendor/Contractor Requirements Construction Updates Find a Provider Careers Nursing Daisy Daisy Winners Bee Award BEE Award Winners Nursing at Thompson Health Nursing at F.F. Thompson Hospital Nursing - Senior Living CNA Apprentice Program CNA Job Openings Physician OB/GYN Physician Opportunities Family Medicine Physician Opportunity Benefits Badge Replacement Student Career Exploration Day 2026 Volunteer Volunteer Application Locations Associate Referral Our Stories Home Careers Home Be Valued. Be Inspired. Be Thompson. If you are looking for a rewarding career with a healthcare provider that... Offers the latest in medical technology and innovative services to deliver excellence Is a benchmark in health care, and the recipient of several prestigious quality awards Values you as an individual and welcomes your ideas for continuous improvement Provides professional development opportunities Has a strong, accountable leadership Is a Magnet-designated hospital, our nurses are an integral part of a prestigious team of healthcare professionals who practice excellence every day. Our RNs in the hospital can participate in our “clinical ladders” or Professional Advancement System (PAS) program to develop their careers. Employs RNs, LPNs and CNAs in our skilled-nursing facility as well as in outpatient practices throughout the system. Our Continuing Care Center even hires GPNs while they work on passing their boards. Offers career advancement opportunities through grants for LPN-to-RN, RN-to-BSN and our tuition assistance program. Has a wonderful residency program for new RN graduates; providing broad training in various clinical specialties over the course of their first year of nursing. ...then you can find it all within Thompson Health! Join our team to make an impact in your life  and in your community! Search Thompson Health's Job Opportunities Nursing Thompson Health nurses hold themselves to the highest standards in caring for others. As a Magnet-designated hospital, our nurses are an integral part of a prestigious team of healthcare professionals who practice excellence every day. Our RNs in the hospital can participate in our clinical ladders program to advance their careers. Our LPNs not only work in our skilled nursing facility, but also in outpatient practices throughout the system. Our Continuing Care Center even hires GPNs while they work on passing their boards. Nursing Opportunities Allied Health / Nursing Support Our allied health and nursing support professionals range from pharmacists, laboratory technologists, radiology technologists, and therapists to certified nursing assistants, patient care technicians, emergency representatives and medical office assistants. For those more entry level roles, we provide training and it is an excellent way to gain clinical work experience. We offer tuition assistance and advancement opportunities. Allied Health / Nursing Support Opportunities Administrative / Business As part of the administrative and business teams you will contribute to our positive, patient-focused culture. From Associate Services (Human Resources) and Corporate Communications professionals to clinical secretaries and receptionists, you’ll keep things running smoothly across the health system and ensure patients and the community receive the best care possible. This is how we have become the premier healthcare provider in the Finger Lakes region. Administrative / Business Opportunities General Support Cafeteria/Nutrition Services, Environmental Services, Facilities, Stock Room, and Security are among the departments within this category. Use your skills to make an impact in your community by doing what you know and love at Thompson Health. Often, it is the small things that make a big difference for patients. These positions are a great way to break into the healthcare field. General Support Opportunities Advance Practice Providers Our Advanced Practice Providers (APPs) have a direct impact on the quality of care we provide to patients. APPs include nurse practitioners, physician assistants, and certified registered nurse anesthetists. We have a strong focus on interdisciplinary collaboration to yield the best possible outcome for the patient. Advance Practice Provider Opportunities Physicians As the premier healthcare provider in the Finger Lakes region, our four-star hospital and award-winning health system is an amazing place to practice medicine, contribute to your community and enjoy a good life. In addition to being an excellent place to work, UR Medicine Thompson Health is located in a beautiful region of Upstate New York with endless family activities and top-ranked schools. Physician Opportunities Browse All Thompson Health Job Opportunities Watch what our Associates have to say about a career at Thompson: Follow us on social media: Our Benefits Our Story Our Mission Our Awards Our Locations Our Community Thompson Health is an equal opportunity employer, encouraging individuals with disabilities & veterans to apply. We can help you find a doctor accepting patients or browse our specialists About Thompson Health About Us News Room Contact Us Find Us Accessibility Vendor/Contractor Requirements Notices of Privacy Practices Reviewer Portal Patient & Visitor Resources Email a Patient / Resident Recognize a Caregiver Make A Gift Calendar of Events Support Groups Price Transparency Careers MyChart Online Bill Pay Find A Doctor Find A Practice Become a Volunteer Notice of Non-Discrimination Policy Follow Us ©2026 Thompson Health 350 Parrish Street Canandaigua, NY 14424 (585) 396-6000 Intranet Email Remote Access (VPN) Terms of Use Login"
    },
    "https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/noyes/about/careers-noyes.aspx": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at Noyes - About Noyes - Noyes Health - URochester Medicine Skip to main content Noyes Health menu About Noyes Welcome to Noyes Quality and Patient Safety Billing & Insurance The People Who Serve You Gift Shop Noyes News More information About Noyes Healthcare Services Urgent Care Medical and Radiation Oncology Noyes Primary Care Orthopaedics Podiatry Medical Imaging Mental Health & Wellness Kidney Disease and Dialysis Physical Therapy and Sports Performance Surgery Pain Management More information on Healthcare Services Community Outreach Are You Expecting? Caregiver Resources Community Health Services Wellness and Outreach Programs More information on Community Outreach Volunteer at Noyes Volunteer Opportunities Noyes Health Auxiliary Give to Noyes More information on Volunteering Careers Give to Noyes Contact Us Phone Numbers Noyes Facilities More information on Contact Us Careers at Noyes Take a Look at Career Opportunities at Noyes Home Current Job Openings Applying to Noyes Benefits Living in Western NY Noyes Health / Careers at Noyes Careers at Noyes Noyes' HR team wants to talk with you about putting your talents to work in our progressive healthcare environment. Noyes offers competitive salaries and excellent benefits. We provide and maintain a fair and competitive salary structure, a cost-effective benefit package, a safe work environment, and a commitment to exceptional patient focus and caring. We're committed to making Noyes a great place to work and a great place to receive care. Our vision, mission, and core values represent our commitment to a culture which enables Noyes to be that place. Current Job Openings To learn more information about a job position, check out one of the sections on our Current Job Openings page. View Job Openings Applying to Noyes To be considered, please complete an online application using the button below. If you are unable to attach your resume to the application, please email your resume to Courtney Galletti . Employment Application Living in Western NY Western NY offers unmatched natural beauty, quality of life, and an abundance of outdoor and recreational activities. Living in Western NY Opportunities for Physicians Noyes is proud to offer an exceptionally supportive and professional environment in which physicians can build vital, successful careers in health care. We offer advanced diagnostic and therapeutic technologies, board-certified doctors trained at top universities, and an emphasis on mentoring and close collaboration between physicians. Noyes Memorial Hospital is a fully accredited 72-bed acute care community hospital located in Dansville, NY, in the heart of the Genesee Valley. Noyes Hospital offers high-quality, comprehensive healthcare services, state-of-the-art imaging systems, 24-hour emergency care, inpatient and outpatient surgical services, intensive care unit, a dedicated telemetry unit, sleep disorders lab, laboratory services, cardiology services, ophthalmology, orthopedics, physical and occupational therapy, and maternity services. Interested physicians are urged to contact Holly Conway, Physician Services to talk about opportunities at Noyes. Currently we are interested in MD Nocturnists, MD Critical Care/Pulmonologists, MD Hospitalist & a Primary Care MD or APP. Phone: (585) 335-4305 Fax: (585) 335-2769 Noyes Health is a \"HPSA designated site\" Noyes Memorial Hospital is an equal opportunity employer. All Noyes properties are tobacco free. Smoking is strictly prohibited on all properties. If you have comments or concerns about your care at Noyes, please contact our Quality Patient Relations Specialist at (585) 335-4388 or email us at noyes-patientrelations@urmc.rochester.edu . If you are not satisfied with the response you receive (if requested), you have the option of contacting the NYSDOH at (585) 423-8100 , or The Joint Commission at email: complaint@jointcommission.org Fax: (630) 792-5636 Mail: Office of Quality Monitoring The Joint Commission One Renaissance Boulevard Oakbrook Terrace, Illinois 60181. Noyes Health Contact Us Careers at Noyes Price Transparency Giving Facebook Twitter General Information Non-Discrimination Policy Language Services & Auxiliary Aids and Services Dansville 111 Clara Barton Street Dansville, NY 14437-9503 (585) 335-6001 Geneseo 50 East South Street Geneseo, NY 14454 (585) 243-9230 ©2026 University of Rochester Medical Center Rochester, NY Intranet Email myURHR Remote Access (VPN) Privacy Topics Viewing: UrmcWebTest"
    },
    "https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/st-james/careers-jobs.aspx": {
      "title": "Careers & Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Careers and Current Job Listings - St. James Hospital - URochester Medicine Skip to main content St. James Hospital menu About St. James Senior Leadership Board of Directors Chair of the Board Letter More information about St. James Services & Specialties General Surgery Laboratory Services Urgent Care Women's Imaging & Breast Center Imaging Services Orthopaedics & Physical Performance More information on our Services & Specialties Patients & Visitors Quality & Safety Patient Relations Visiting Hours & Restrictions Locations & Maps Food Services & Cafeteria MyChart Billing & Insurance Gift Shop More information on Patients & Visitors News & Events Find a Provider Contact Us Giving About SJM Foundation Foundation Board of Directors More information on Giving to St. James Careers Join Our Legacy View Current Openings Home About St. James Services & Specialties Patients & Visitors News & Events Find a Provider Contact Us Giving St. James Hospital / Careers & Job Opportunities Careers & Job Opportunities St. James Hospital Benefits Our employees enjoy a comprehensive benefit plan, including the following: Health, Dental, and Vision Plan Competitive 401k Retirement Plan With Matching Contribution Short-Term and Long-Term Disability Comprehensive Training Programs Educational Discounts for Employees Generous Paid Time Off (PTO) and Paid Sick time Training Reimbursement Life Insurance Accidental Death and Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account 529 College Savings Program Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Hiring RN Graduates! Nurse Residency Program . View Current Openings Our Human Resource Team Kelsie Acor, HR Manager Jessica Cartwright, HR Assistant If you have any questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources at SJHHR@urmc.rochester.edu . widget-6742b0b3-50b Our EEO Policy St. James Hospital does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, domestic violence victim status, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, military/veteran status, national origin, race, religion/creed, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, or any other status protected by law in matters of employment, volunteering, or activities. St. James Hospital is a proud recipient of the Silver Level American Heart Association Workplace Wellbeing Scorecard. St. James Hospital is a proud recipient of the Patriot Award by the New York Employer Support of The Guard and Reserve. St. James Hospital Staff Testimonials Hear what our employees have to say about our work environment. St. James Hospital Contact Us Location & Maps Find a Doctor Quality & Safety Compliance & Privacy Price Transparency Address 7329 Seneca Road North Hornell, NY 14843 Phone Number (607) 247-2200 Email SJHInformation@URMC.Rochester.edu Connect with Us ©2026 University of Rochester Medical Center Rochester, NY Intranet Email myURHR Remote Access (VPN) Privacy Topics Viewing: UrmcWebTest"
    },
    "https://www.flhealth.org/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | Finger Lakes Health Skip to main content Search Search the site for providers, locations, and content. Dismiss Modal Close Providers Locations Services Patients & Visitors Online Bill Pay Patient Portal Careers Patients & Visitors Community Resources search Schedule Appointment show off canvas menu Close Schedule Appointment In this section Back Main Menu Online Bill Pay Patient Portal Careers Patients & Visitors Community Resources Providers Locations Services Patients & Visitors Home Careers Careers In this section Back Careers CNA Program Apply for the CNA Program Advancement Opportunities Curriculum General Information Program Overview Job Listings Excellus Employee Coverage Provider Recruitment Nursing Healing Environment Seeking a Healthcare Career? . . . Let Us Introduce Ourselves! By selecting University of Rochester Medicine Finger Lakes Health you will be joining an organization with the Vision to be the Best Health Care Network of our size in the U.S. and an Employer of Choice . We encourage and support initiative and the personal and professional growth of our people. As an employee of Finger Lakes Health, your colleagues model our Values of Service, Teamwork, Dignity, Respect, Responsibility and Vision. We offer a competitive salary and opportunity to select benefits that meet your personal needs. This flexible benefit package includes medical, dental, and life insurance, tuition assistance, on-site Child Care Center (Geneva) and more for full and part time employees. Visit our Where We Are page for location information. Career opportunities are available at our three main campuses in the Finger Lakes region. Candidates are encouraged to view these opportunities by clicking on the category for more detailed job opening information. If you are interested in joining our health system please apply online. If you need assistance completing an online application or need access to a computer, you are invited to visit the Human Resources Department in Geneva or Penn Yan, New York. The Geneva office is located at 789 Pre-Emption Road, Finger Lakes Health Commons; The Penn Yan office is located at Soldiers & Sailors Hospital at 418 North Main Street. Please contact the Human Resources Team at (315) 787-4039 if you need additional assistance. Thank you for your interest in employment with Finger Lakes Health. To view all open positions, click here . Download our benefits package for review. Footer Menu About Us About Us Contact Us Hospital Visitation Maps and Directions Mission, Vision, Values Patient Portals Privacy Careers / Education Careers Provider Recruitment Nursing Education FLH College of Nursing & Health Sciences Marion S. Whelan School of Practical Nursing Community Outreach Community Health Needs Assessment, Community Service Plan and Community Health Improvement Plan Events Listen to a Podcast Make a Donation News Report to the Community Thrive Magazine Patient Billing Price Transparency Resources Price Transparency - Geneva General Hospital Price Transparency - Soldiers and Sailors Memorial Hospital Patient Financial Services Financial Aid Program Good Faith Estimate No Surprises Act Participating Health Plans Pay Your Bill Online Facebook Flickr Intragram Youtube Copyright © 2026 UR Medicine Finger Lakes Health 196 North Street, Geneva, NY 14456"
    },
